19:    Stamp the whole 3x3 input tile into the 9x9 output at positions marked by the least frequent input color.
21:    Input structure:
22:    - A 3x3 grid with no black pixels; black is reserved for the output background.
23:    - Exactly one color has the smallest pixel count.
25:    Rule:
26:    - Find the unique least frequent color in the input.
27:    - Build a 3-by-3 array of 3x3 blocks on a black canvas.
28:    - For each input cell of the least frequent color, copy the entire input grid
29:      into the corresponding output block; leave all other blocks black.
31:    Key insight:
32:    - The rare-color mask selects whole-tile positions; output cells are not scaled
33:      input pixels.
34:    """
35:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
36:    assert g.ndim == 2 and g.shape == (3, 3), "expected a 3x3 input grid"
37:    assert not np.any(g == Color.BLACK), "black is the output background color"
